+### Ordinary generated blocking variable stores (P4 review proposal)
+
+**Scope.** Decide at each blocking store in the original instruction order.
+Admit a packed integral variable whose physical element is at most 64 bits,
+with fixed element and whole width or an in-bounds fixed slice. Verify the
+alias mapping and exclude nets, driver backing, NBA and dynamic selections.
+Multiple outputs, ordinary CombAt dispatch and membership in a cycle do not
+affect this per-site decision. Evaluate RHS and address exactly once.
+
+**Equality.** Use the ordinary ABI input *after assignment conversion*. Expand
+the whole-element width sentinel first. Let M contain exactly the selected
+destination bits; handle a width of 64 without shifting by 64. Align the
+right-justified source planes to M, merge them into the old element and keep
+all unselected bits. For four-state storage compare both a and b, including
+the distinction between X and Z. In approximate `--state=2` on a declared
+four-state element, first use `a = a & ~b, b = 0` for the source, then merge
+and compare both resulting planes to storage. For a declared two-state
+element compare its single plane after conversion. On equality charge exactly
+one `slot.writes` with the normal counter semantics. On difference or decline,
+hand the original arguments to the canonical write while the old element and
+counts are intact. Preserve `slot.changes`, wake and registration counts,
+SCC iteration accounting, and the return/stop prefix.
+
+**Live observers.** Admission requires initialized storage and observer tables
+and a current binding under §4.2 of RUNTIME_ABI. For each store, apply every
+applicable row. A decline takes the ordinary path before any direct effect.
+
+| Current state | Rule for the initial fixed-range W |
+| --- | --- |
+| Ordinary `@(...)`, posedge or negedge subscription | Admit when matching depends only on an actual transition in the watched range. Equality leaves every waiter armed. Changes go through the original edge matcher and queue order. |
+| `iff` on an ordinary edge or change | Admit only if the existing matcher invokes the guard after a matching transition. On equality it never calls the guard. On a change the kernel evaluates it at the write position, before later instructions, with the original values and disarm/re-arm behavior. Decline an expression monitor or unclassified guard. |
+| `$monitor`, expression waits, sampled/clocking or module-path monitors | Decline a slot feeding such a live observer and ambiguous aliases. Preserve the original sampling region, callbacks and scheduled output. |
+| VCD/FST waveform | Permit a regular end-of-slot snapshot that reads the canonical store. Initial snapshots and dump-control commands keep their scheduled position. Decline when per-transition/glitch capture is configured; revalidate on mode changes. |
+| VPI or foreign access | Decline while VPI is enabled, or when a foreign alias can observe or alter the slot with no validated invalidation. Keep callback registration, delivery and deposits on the kernel path. |
+| Race inspection or order exploration | Decline while active so the original access and ordering information reaches the diagnostic path. |
+| Force/release, procedural assign/deassign, held or strength-owned storage | Decline if the slot is marked held or can update a hidden/base value. Equal visible bits alone cannot predict the value after release. |
+| Nested notification, outstanding observer walk/drain, event-controlled NBA observer, other unresolved effects | Decline unless the initial contract above explicitly admits the state. Preserve every intermediate transition, including A→B→A. |
+
+Keep the existing post-write ending test and SIGINT/checkpoints in the W-only
+control. Direct RHS reads and a cheaper post-write ending test have independent
+experimental controls. Every variant must observe termination at the same point.
+
+In `--tier-check` exercise admitted W on private state. From identical inputs
+compare the generated and VM ordered attempts (including equality), element,
+slice, RHS, normalized old/new planes, counters, observation/queue order and
+stop point. Replay synchronous observer effects needed by a following read or
+stop, or decline before borrowing. Report the actual direct/declined path
+separately from semantic agreement. Publish once via the reference path.
+Overflow, incomplete traces or a mismatch fail the check. Execute modules
+contain no recording code.
 
