+#### Ordinary variable-site access (proposed service 20, version 1)
+
+Use `query_service(20, 1)` on the current activation's kernel table.
+Service 20 is independent of fusion service 19 v1. The existing ABI 0.5
+query mechanism and module descriptor v1 suffice: the ordinary resume
+contains its canonical fallback and therefore omits this optional accelerator
+from the mandatory requirements list. An absent or truncated table selects
+that fallback. The following C layout uses the ABI's native calling convention,
+natural alignment and fixed-width types.
+
+```c
+#define KIRIMA_SERVICE_VARIABLE_SITE 20u
+#define KIRIMA_VARIABLE_SITE_VERSION 1u
+enum kirima_site_status { KIRIMA_SITE_OK, KIRIMA_SITE_DECLINED, KIRIMA_SITE_INVALID };
+typedef struct kirima_site_v1 {
+    uint32_t sir_slot, element, lsb, width;       /* explicit positive width */
+    uint32_t element_width, domain;              /* declared physical layout */
+} kirima_site_v1;
+typedef struct kirima_site_view_v1 {
+    const uint64_t *observation_epoch;
+    uint64_t bound_observation_epoch;
+    const uint64_t *element_words;               /* canonical a[, b] */
+} kirima_site_view_v1;
+typedef struct kirima_site_batch_v1 {
+    const uint64_t *storage_epoch;
+    uint64_t bound_storage_epoch;
+    const kirima_site_view_v1 *views;            /* one per input descriptor */
+    uint64_t *logical_slot_writes;
+    const uint32_t *ending;                      /* 0 or 1 */
+    void *lease;                                 /* host-owned */
+} kirima_site_batch_v1;
+typedef struct kirima_site_api_v1 {
+    uint32_t table_bytes;
+    uint32_t (*borrow)(kirima_context *, uint32_t process, uint32_t sir_process_row,
+                       const kirima_site_v1 *, uint32_t count, kirima_site_batch_v1 *);
+    void (*release)(kirima_context *, kirima_site_batch_v1 *);
+} kirima_site_api_v1;
+```
+
+- **Binding.** The module supplies immutable site descriptors in deterministic
+  SIR instruction order. On the registered runtime process and verified SIR
+  process row, the host validates the fixed blocking store, owner, physical
+  alias, true variable kind, element, slice, domain, width, stride, state mode
+  and current observer policy. Width is explicit even for a whole-element
+  descriptor. A successful borrow supplies one view per descriptor; a declined
+  site has a zero bound observation epoch. A normal optimization decline has no
+  effects. A malformed descriptor or foreign owner is INVALID and fails module
+  validation/execution. Release exactly once on every exit from a successful
+  borrow. Declined/invalid requests acquire no lease.
+- **Lifetime.** A lease belongs to one active resume, one Context and one
+  thread. A nested resume has a separate lease. The host keeps the view array,
+  epoch cells and the read-only ending cell address-stable until release.
+  Every direct access starts by comparing the nonzero bound storage and
+  observation epochs with these stable cells. Before a storage/layout move
+  or counter-table reallocation the host invalidates storage epochs; before
+  an observer is added, removed or changes eligibility, or a force/hold or
+  global observation mode changes, it invalidates the affected observation
+  epochs. Exhaustion disables the affected access; epochs never wrap to a
+  previously valid value. The equality comparison and increment run in one
+  uninterrupted segment without a host call. An element or counter pointer is
+  usable only inside such a validated segment. Following a host call (including
+  a write, checkpoint or callback), start a fresh validation through the stable
+  cells before touching storage again. On a mismatch use the canonical service
+  or acquire a fresh lease. Release before suspend, frame destruction or
+  return. Raw signal values cannot be reused across a callback.
+- **Accounting and termination.** On equality increment the host's live
+  unsigned 64-bit logical write counter once, with ordinary counter semantics.
+  On a change or decline the canonical service owns the whole write. Keep
+  bookkeeping visible before any observer, reentry or stop. The ending cell
+  equals `kernel->ending(ctx)` at each original post-write test, including
+  immediately after a callback. It is not the pending SIGINT flag and reading
+  it does not consume an interrupt. W alone retains the existing ending call;
+  using this cell is a separately measured variant. Check mode supplies
+  shadow-owned storage, generations, counter and ending state and compares
+  writes as specified in CODEGEN_SPEC.
+- **Cache identity.** For every site-aware ordinary module, including designs
+  with zero fused islands, extend the §2 key with a versioned site emitter,
+  canonical SIR and schema, verified physical layout, analysis identity and
+  options, descriptor content, service ID/version (20,1), state mode, bounds,
+  limits and observation options affecting emitted code, and explicit
+  `execute` or `check`. Preserve the generated-source and public-header
+  hashes, compiler/version/flags, ABI and target. Runtime addresses, leases
+  and epoch values are never serialized into the cache. Validate against the
+  current Context on load/bind. Test cold/warm and execute/check in either
+  order and load the same artifact into two independent Contexts.
 
